08: don't crash on BLE scan results when BLUETOOTH_CONNECT is missing (2026-11)

On Android 12+, BluetoothDevice.getName()/getType() need BLUETOOTH_CONNECT.
BLEClient.onLeScan called them unguarded on a binder thread, so a scan with
only BLUETOOTH_SCAN granted threw an uncaught SecurityException and killed
the app on Search (Galaxy Tab A7 Lite, Android 14, de1app 1.46.1.215).
The device is now reported without a name instead. The Tcl side
(de1app#378) also stops scanning without the permission.

libs/ble.jar is a PREBUILT jar of this source: after applying this patch,
run mods/08-rebuild-ble-jar.sh or the fix is not in the APK.

--- a/ble/src/tk/tcl/wish/BLEClient.java	2026-11-20 12:52:17
+++ b/ble/src/tk/tcl/wish/BLEClient.java	2026-11-20 12:52:17
@@ -769,10 +769,24 @@
 
     public void onLeScan(BluetoothDevice device, int rssi, byte[] scanRecord) {
 	if (device != null) {
+	    /*
+	     * Android 12+: getName() (and getType()) need BLUETOOTH_CONNECT.
+	     * Without it they throw SecurityException on this binder thread,
+	     * which is uncaught and kills the app. Report the device without
+	     * a name instead (Decent, 2026-11: crash on Search).
+	     */
+	    String name = null;
+	    int type = BluetoothDevice.DEVICE_TYPE_UNKNOWN;
+	    try {
+		name = device.getName();
+		type = device.getType();
+	    } catch (SecurityException e) {
+		Log.w("BLEClient", "scan callback: no BLUETOOTH_CONNECT, " +
+		      "can't read device name: " + e);
+	    }
 	    Log.i("BLEClient", "scan callback: " + device.getAddress() + " " +
-		  device.getName());
-	    nativeScanResult(id, device.getAddress(), device.getName(),
-			     device.getType(), rssi);
+		  name);
+	    nativeScanResult(id, device.getAddress(), name, type, rssi);
 	}
     }
 
